# Admin Panel Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and configure your values

# Backend API URL - required for admin operations
# For local development use the localhost backend:
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5000

# For production (Render or other hosting) use the deployed backend URL:
# Uncomment and set this when deploying to production:
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://kharido-backend.onrender.com

# Important Notes and Deployment Instructions:
# 1. The URL should NOT have a trailing slash (e.g. use https://example.com, NOT https://example.com/).
# 2. The URL should NOT include the /api suffix — the admin app adds the /api path automatically.
# 3. Use https:// for production and http:// for local development when appropriate.
# 4. Ensure the backend server is running and accessible at this URL.
# 5. For debugging 404 or CORS errors, verify this value exactly matches your backend deployment URL.
#
# Updating this value for different environments:
# - Local development: copy this file to .env.local and leave VITE_BACKEND_URL pointing to http://localhost:5000
# - Production (Render, Vercel, etc.): set VITE_BACKEND_URL in your host's dashboard/environment variables
#   (do not commit production secrets or URLs to source control; use the hosting provider's env settings).
# - When switching environments, ensure you rebuild the admin front-end so the new VITE_BACKEND_URL is embedded.
#
# Example (Render dashboard):
# - Key: VITE_BACKEND_URL
# - Value: https://kharido-backend.onrender.com
# Note: Render and other hosts will provide the environment to the build/runtime; do not include /api suffix here.
#
# If you need to support multiple backend environments simultaneously, manage environment-specific .env files
# (e.g. .env.development, .env.production) or set the variables via your CI/CD/deployment platform.